src('SRC049','Report on the Historical Record of U.S. Government Involvement with Unidentified Anomalous Phenomena (UAP), Volume I (DOPSR-2024-0263)','DoD All-domain Anomaly Resolution Office (AARO)','U.S. Department of Defense','2024-03-08 (report dated Feb 2024)','Official government report','PRIMARY','https://documents2.theblackvault.com/documents/dod/AARO_Historical_Record_Report_Volume_1_2024.pdf','DOPSR-2024-0263','64 pp; nuclear-related passage ~pp.29-33 (text lines 1209-1355 of my pdftotext)','%s'%A,'INC019;INC020;EVD090;CLM039','Secondary Narrative on UAP near nuclear facilities; five interviewees at Malmstrom, Ellsworth, Vandenberg and Minot (1966-77); claims of launch control facilities offline or total power failure; no UAP-specific NDAs found; the 1964 reentry-vehicle film not recovered, time/place correlated with an anti-ballistic-missile test; remaining allegations deferred to Volume II; sources cited as "AARO case files" (not public).','Primary for AARO’s own stated position; mirror copy from The Black Vault (not aaro.mil).','VERIFIED','EXAMINED')
ev('EVD090',"AARO Volume I (SRC049), the primary AARO text, says nothing on the cause of the Echo or Oscar shutdowns and does not mention transformers, electrical storms or an EMP test. Its nuclear passage: five former USAF members who served near ICBM silos at Malmstrom, Ellsworth, Vandenberg and Minot (1966-77) claim sightings and/or UAP disruption (launch control facilities offline or total power failure); AARO 'investigated and reached conclusions on the majority of the claims'; unresolved allegations deferred to Volume II; only one nuclear-related item is addressed in the findings (the alleged 1964 reentry-vehicle film, not recovered, matched in time/place to an ABM test). It also reports no UAP-specific NDAs found in the records AARO reviewed (apart from standard Title 18 language) - which bears on, but does not refute, the claim that Salas, Meiwald and others signed OSI NDAs (those may be ordinary debrief statements and AARO's search covers only what it found). So the 'transformer cascade' and 'EMP test' statements (EVD089) were made in interviews/press, not in Volume I; Volume II was due later and I could not confirm it exists or what it says. Footnote 98 cites 'AARO case files' (non-public).",'GOVERNMENT_RECORD','SRC049','INC019;INC020;EVD089;CLM039','10099','HIGH','VERIFIED')
miss('MIS052','AARO Historical Record Report Volume II (if published) and AARO case files cited in Vol I footnotes 98-109 (Malmstrom interviewee case files)','SUSPECTED','AARO','Check aaro.mil and request via FOIA/Mandatory declassification',10099)
